area: fetch
case: 44-window-cap-negative
verification: explicit-divergence
oracle: python
projection: fetch
reason: not reachable through the tool surface — Model.fetch_request_of_yojson checks offset ≥ 0 and max_chars is the config constant (Default or Uncapped) — so this pins Fetcher.window_text's own boundary. Python's slice clamps or wraps a negative index: the oracle answers text taken from the end (negative offset) or a window at least partly past the end (negative cap). The port raises Invalid_argument from Array.sub on a negative offset and returns an empty window on a negative cap. Recorded as a library-boundary difference, raised in the plan rather than fixed: lib/** is outside this corpus's ownership.
--- oracle
window= hello worl\n\n[...]
more=true
--- port
window= 
more=true
